  "solution": {
    "text": "When salicylic acid reacts with acetic anhydride in the presence of conc. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}$ and heat, the product will be $(Q)$ acetyl salicylic acid $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{9} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\mathrm{O}_{4}\\right)$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0006_280d04db25eb.png\">\r\nSo, the option (a) is correct answer."
